# Fix Desktop Navigation Freeze on Consecutive Page Clicks

## Problem Description
When clicking two pages consecutively (e.g. Dashboard &rarr; All Letters, or rapid consecutive clicks on any desktop nav link), the UI freezes completely and stops responding to clicks until the browser URL is manually refreshed. This issue occurs in desktop/normal view and does not happen in mobile view.

## Root Cause Analysis
1. **Next.js 14 App Router Action Queue Deadlock**:
   - Next.js 14.2 `<Link>` components intercept clicks with `e.preventDefault()` and dispatch a `NAVIGATE` action to Next.js's internal `actionQueue` inside React's `startTransition`.
   - When a user clicks one page and then clicks another link before the first transition settles, Next.js marks the first action as `discarded`.
   - In Next.js 14.2's `action-queue.js`, discarded actions return immediately without calling `action.resolve()` or `action.reject()`.
   - Because the first action's deferred promise is never settled, React 18's transition scheduler stays pending indefinitely.
   - Once stuck, any subsequent click on any `<Link>` has `e.preventDefault()` called by Next.js, but the router never navigates—making the page appear completely frozen.
2. **Why Mobile View Did Not Freeze**:
   - On mobile, navigation links reside inside a slide-out drawer that immediately closes on click (`setMobileMenuOpen(false)`). The user cannot click consecutive links while a transition is pending. On desktop, all 5 navigation links are simultaneously visible side-by-side.
3. **`useSearchParams` and `<Suspense>` De-optimization**:
   - Client pages (`letters`, `search`, `settings`, `letters/[id]`) were using `useSearchParams()`, forcing them into `<Suspense>` boundaries. In Next.js App Router, in-flight transitions interrupted while resolving Suspense boundaries exacerbate client-side router deadlocks.

